@page "/browser-options"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http

<PageTitle>Configure client from server</PageTitle>

<h1>Configure Blazor client behavior from the server (.NET 11)</h1>

<p class="lead">
    Blazor apps can configure client-side startup behavior from the server in C# when
    mapping Razor components, instead of hand-writing <code>Blazor.start</code> JavaScript
    (<a href="https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/67337" target="_blank">#67337</a>).
</p>

<p>This app configures the following in <code>Program.cs</code> with <code>WithBrowserOptions</code>:</p>

<pre><code class="language-csharp">app.MapRazorComponents&lt;App&gt;()
    .AddInteractiveServerRenderMode()
    .WithBrowserOptions(options =&gt;
    {
        options.LogLevel = LogLevel.Debug;
        options.Server.ReconnectionMaxRetries = 10;
        options.Server.ReconnectionRetryInterval = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(1.5);
        options.Ssr.PreserveDom = true;
    });</code></pre>

@if (resolved is not null)
{
    <h2>Resolved options for this request</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">Read on the server with <code>HttpContext.GetBrowserOptions()</code>.</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>LogLevel:</strong> @resolved.LogLevel</li>
        <li><strong>Server.ReconnectionMaxRetries:</strong> @resolved.Server.ReconnectionMaxRetries</li>
        <li><strong>Server.ReconnectionRetryInterval:</strong> @resolved.Server.ReconnectionRetryInterval</li>
        <li><strong>Ssr.PreserveDom:</strong> @resolved.Ssr.PreserveDom</li>
    </ul>
}

<div class="alert alert-info">
    <strong>What this shows:</strong> the options above are the client startup settings this app
    configured in C# with <code>WithBrowserOptions</code> — no <code>Blazor.start</code>
    JavaScript. To watch one take effect at runtime, stop and restart the server: the
    reconnection UI retries using the configured interval and retry count.
</div>

@code {
    // Static SSR page (no @rendermode) so HttpContext is available to read the
    // resolved options the server serialized into the page.
    [CascadingParameter] public HttpContext? HttpContext { get; set; }

    BrowserOptions? resolved;

    protected override void OnInitialized() => resolved = HttpContext?.GetBrowserOptions();
}
